    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with a standout 87.14 efficiency score. His matchup against Feltner is the premier spot of the day, as he benefits from a favorable SP_xERA of 4.96 and a prime batting order position that elevates his ceiling for both counting stats and the stolen bases our squad desperately needs. Alongside him, **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **Gabriel Moreno** (71.10) provide significant value; **Mickey Moniak** specifically leverages a massive 14% platoon edge against Kelly, making him an essential high-floor play despite his typical middle-order slot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card was the final UTIL spot, where **Austin Riley** (58.74) narrowly edged out the bench options. While **Tyler Soderstrom** sits at 57.87, he is fighting through a difficult matchup against the elite arm of Rasmussen (3.17 xERA), which heavily suppresses his raw projection. We are opting to lean into **Austin Riley**'s positional flexibility, though we remain wary of his lower order placement and the modest 4.62 xERA of Thornton. Meanwhile, **Max Muncy** (42.29) and **Henry Bolte** (41.35) are essentially at their floor today, tethered to the lineup primarily because of the park factors in their favor, but they remain at high risk of being swapped out if we need to preserve games later in the week.\n\nWe continue to monitor the status of our bench depth, specifically **Jose Caballero**, who remains our primary contingency if any late-scratch lineup shuffles occur. With **James Wood**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** locked into the IL, our roster flexibility is strained. While players like **Trevor Story**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana** are available, none currently possess the projected efficiency to override the starters in today's specific favorable matchups. Keep a close eye on the weather and late-inning bullpen usage, as the volatility of these matchups against Rasmussen and Warren makes bench management critical for our Roto standing.",
